00:12:20,300 --> 00:12:21,770
I'm not in san francisco.

260
00:12:21,830 --> 00:12:22,830
I'm on a train.

261
00:12:22,900 --> 00:12:24,700
Were you even listening to me?

262
00:12:24,770 --> 00:12:26,730
Uh, no, I was talking to my friend, but what's up?

263
00:12:26,800 --> 00:12:28,770
What's up? I'll tell you what's up.

264
00:12:28,830 --> 00:12:30,070
I'm in a crisis situation,

265
00:12:30,070 --> 00:12:32,820
And I need you to marshal your powers of concentration,

266
00:12:32,820 --> 00:12:34,200
Limited as they may be...

267
00:12:34,270 --> 00:12:36,600
Give me the phone.

268
00:12:36,670 --> 00:12:38,330
Hi, penny. it's leonard.

269
00:12:38,400 --> 00:12:39,470
Hey, leonard.

270
00:12:39,530 --> 00:12:42,000
What's going on with dr. wackadoodle?

271
00:12:42,070 --> 00:12:44,630
He's calling to ask you a favor.

272
00:12:44,700 --> 00:12:48,460
You might be confused because he didn't use the words, "penny," "sheldon,

273
00:12:48,460 --> 00:12:49,670
" "please" or "favor."

274
00:12:49,730 --> 00:12:50,900
Okay.

275
00:12:50,970 --> 00:12:52,100
Enough chitchat.

276
00:12:52,170 --> 00:12:53,370
Okay, step one.

277
00:12:53,430 --> 00:12:55,930
Locate your emergency key to our apartment.

278
00:12:56,000 --> 00:12:58,770
Step two, enter our apartment.

279
00:12:58,830 --> 00:13:00,500
Step three...

280
00:13:01,500 --> 00:13:02,930
Enter my bedroom.

281
00:13:03,000 --> 00:13:04,200
Step four...

282
00:13:04,270 --> 00:13:06,300
Oh, hang on, sheldon, getting another call.

283
00:13:06,370 --> 00:13:07,530
No!

284
00:13:07,600 --> 00:13:08,970
Leonard, let me tell you something.

285
00:13:09,030 --> 00:13:11,000
Personal robots cannot get here soon enough.

286
00:13:13,770 --> 00:13:18,170
And that bright little star peeking her head out early today...

287
00:13:18,230 --> 00:13:20,230
That's venus.

288
00:13:20,300 --> 00:13:22,070
That is so cool.

289
00:13:22,130 --> 00:13:24,200
You really know a lot about space.

290
00:13:24,270 --> 00:13:25,330
Come on.

291
00:13:25,400 --> 00:13:30,530
When you were on tv in firefly, you were actually in space.

292
00:13:30,600 --> 00:13:33,270
You're not one of those guys who really believe that, are you?

293
00:13:33,330 --> 00:13:36,100
You mean one of the hopeless geeks?

294
00:13:36,170 --> 00:13:37,330
No.

295
00:13:37,400 --> 00:13:38,870
Those are crazy people.

296
00:13:41,970 --> 00:13:45,330
Howard, be a dear and get me another one of these.

297
00:13:50,470 --> 00:13:53,100
Now, him, he's one of those geeks.

298
00:13:54,300 --> 00:13:57,730
All right, now, before you enter my bedroom unescorted,

299
00:13:57,730 --> 00:14:00,460
I need you to understand that this onetime

300
00:14:00,460 --> 00:14:03,970
Grant of access does not create a permanent easement.

301
00:14:04,030 --> 00:14:05,670
Easement.

302
00:14:07,470 --> 00:14:08,930
It's a legal right of access.

303
00:14:09,000 --> 00:14:10,330
Good grief.

304
00:14:11,700 --> 00:14:12,830
What?

305
00:14:12,900 --> 00:14:14,200
No, don't put me on hold.

306
00:14:14,270 --> 00:14:15,670
Oh!

307
00:14:16,700 --> 00:14:18,270
Do you believe him?

308
00:14:18,330 --> 00:14:23,330
Normally around women, he has the personality of a boiled potato.

309
00:14:23,400 --> 00:14:26,800
Put one beer in him, and he's m. night charmalarmalon.

310
00:14:29,500 --> 00:14:31,730
Is that what he's drinking?

311
00:14:31,800 --> 00:14:32,800
It's not even real beer.

312
00:14:32,870 --> 00:14:34,170
What? look at it.

313
00:14:34,230 --> 00:14:36,570
"non-alcoholic beer."

314
00:14:38,570 --> 00:14:39,670
What's going on?

315
00:14:39,730 --> 00:14:40,900
I don't know.

316
00:14:40,970 --> 00:14:43,430
Some sort of placebo effect, I guess.

317
00:14:43,500 --> 00:14:46,230
Placebo, you say.

318
00:14:46,300 --> 00:14:48,970
Interesting.

319
00:14:49,030 --> 00:14:51,370
Yes, I'm still here. where am I going? I'm on a train.

320
00:14:51,430 --> 00:14:51,630
Now,

321
00:14:51,630 --> 00:14:55,430
What you'll be looking for is a small wooden box located

322
00:14:55,430 --> 00:15:00,330
Between a hoberman's sphere and a sample of quartz flecked with pyrite.

323
00:15:00,400 --> 00:15:02,130
Hoberman's sphere.

324
00:15:02,200 --> 00:15:04,870
It's collapsible icosidodecahedron.

325
00:15:06,330 --> 00:15:09,000
No, the thing with the time on it is my alarm clock.

326
00:15:12,130 --> 00:15:15,700
Actually, in india, the names of constellations are different.

327
00:15:15,770 --> 00:15:20,670
Where you have the big dipper, we have the big curry pot.

328
00:15:20,730 --> 00:15:22,600
You're making that up.

329
00:15:22,670 --> 00:15:24,700
You got me.

330
00:15:24,770 --> 00:15:27,400
Now what are you going to do with me?

331
00:15:31,400 --> 00:15:32,970
Raj. yes?

332
00:15:33,030 --> 00:15:34,530
Look. what am I looking at?

333
00:15:34,600 --> 00:15:35,600
You tell me.

334
00:15:35,670 --> 00:15:38,570
"non-alcoholic beer."

335
00:15:46,470 --> 00:15:50,530
Hi. I'm the small package good things come in.

336
00:15:53,270 --> 00:15:57,030
Okay, I got a box, but there's no key in here. just letters.

337
00:15:57,100 --> 00:15:58,800
That's the wrong box. put it back.

338
00:15:58,870 --> 00:16:01,730
Oh, sheldon, are these letters from your grandmother?

339
00:16:01,800 --> 00:16:03,300
Don't read those letters!

340
00:16:03,370 --> 00:16:05,470
Oh, look, she calls you "moon pie."

341
00:16:05,530 --> 00:16:06,600
That is so cute.

342
00:16:06,670 --> 00:16:08,670
Put down the letters!

343
00:16:11,100 --> 00:16:13,900
Hey, penny. it's leonard.

344
00:16:13,970 --> 00:16:15,100
Hey, leonard. how's the train ride?

345
00:16:15,170 --> 00:16:17,630
Delightful.

346
00:16:17,700 --> 00:16:19,520
Listen, I don't know what you're doing right now,

347
00:16:19,520 --> 00:16:22,300
But there are little bubbles forming on the corners of sheldon's mouth.

348
00:16:22,370 --> 00:16:24,400
Okay, yeah, I kind of crossed a line.

349
00:16:24,470 --> 00:16:25,400
Put him back on.

350
00:16:25,470 --> 00:16:26,800
Thank you.

351
00:16:26,870 --> 00:16:28,770
I'm back.

352
00:16:28,830 --> 00:16:30,900
What up, moon pie?

353
00:16:30,970 --> 00:16:34,130
Nobody calls me moon pie but meemaw!

354
00:16:35,970 --> 00:16:38,830
Hey, penny. leonard again.

355
00:16:40,200 --> 00:16:43,900
So anyway, in the dream, you and I were ice skating, just the two of us.

356
00:16:43,970 --> 00:16:44,730
And then,

357
00:16:44,930 --> 00:16:47,580
I picked you up by your ankles and twirled

358
00:16:47,580 --> 00:16:50,930
You round and round until your legs tore off.

359
00:16:52,970 --> 00:16:56,600
I tried to stick them back on, but before I could,

360
00:16:56,600 --> 00:17:00,530
You turned into a giant loaf of pumpernickel bread.

361
00:17:01,600 --> 00:17:03,030
What do you think that means?

362
00:17:04,370 --> 00:17:06,370
I really don't know.

363
00:17:07,770 --> 00:17:09,300
I'll give you a little clue.

364
00:17:09,370 --> 00:17:10,400
My favorite sandwich?

365
00:17:10,470 --> 00:17:12,830
Salami on pumpernickel.

366
00:17:12,900 --> 00:17:14,900
Is that so?

367
00:17:16,030 --> 00:17:17,500
And did you know the word "pumpernickel"

368
00:17:17,570 --> 00:17:19,700
Comes from the german words "pumper" and "nickel,"

369
00:17:19,770 --> 00:17:22,200
Which loosely translates to "fart goblin"?

370
00:17:24,230 --> 00:17:26,230
No. I didn't.

371
00:17:29,730 --> 00:17:31,800
Okay, I found the box. now what?

372
00:17:31,870 --> 00:17:34,520
You're holding a japanese puzzle box,

373
00:17:34,520 --> 00:17:37,470
Which takes ten precise moves to open.

374
00:17:37,530 --> 00:17:37,870
First,

375
00:17:37,870 --> 00:17:41,020
Locate the panel with the diamond pattern and

376
00:17:41,020 --> 00:17:44,730
Slide the center portion one millimeter to the left.

377
00:17:44,800 --> 00:17:47,310
Then, on the opposite end of the box,

378
00:17:47,310 --> 00:17:50,530
Slide the entire panel down two millimeters.

379
00:17:50,600 --> 00:17:52,300
You'll hear a slight click.

380
00:17:52,370 --> 00:17:56,130
Hang on. sheldon, do you have any emotional attachment to this box?

381
00:17:56,200 --> 00:17:58,000
No, it's a novelty I ordered off the internet.

382
00:17:58,070 --> 00:17:59,700
Did you hear the click?

383
00:17:59,770 --> 00:18:01,770
Not yet.

384
00:18:05,000 --> 00:18:06,630
There it is.

385
00:18:10,190 --> 00:18:11,660
Okay, here's another one.

386
00:18:11,760 --> 00:18:16,040
If you married the famous rock guitarist johnny winter,

387
00:18:16,040 --> 00:18:18,030
You'd be summer winter.

388
00:18:19,860 --> 00:18:21,490
Uh-huh. yep.

389
00:18:22,990 --> 00:18:26,930
Okay, I'm going to just go for broke here and say I like you.

390
00:18:26,990 --> 00:18:29,760
Yeah?

391
00:18:31,660 --> 00:18:35,040
Do you realistically see any conversational path that would take me from

392
00:18:35,040 --> 00:18:36,610
Where we are right now to a place

393
00:18:36,610 --> 00:18:38,760
Where I could ask you out and you'd say yes?

394
00:18:40,190 --> 00:18:41,530
No.

395
00:18:43,060 --> 00:18:44,830
Fair enough.

396
00:18:44,890 --> 00:18:46,090
I'll leave you in peace.

397
00:18:46,160 --> 00:18:48,160
Thank you.

398
00:18:50,190 --> 00:18:51,390
But before I go,

399
00:18:51,390 --> 00:18:54,110
Would you mind if I just take one

400
00:18:54,110 --> 00:18:57,830
Picture of us together for my facebook page?

401
00:18:57,890 --> 00:18:59,460
Sure.

402
00:19:08,460 --> 00:19:10,160
Okay. great.

403
00:19:10,230 --> 00:19:12,830
Now, can I take one where it looks like we're making out?

404
00:19:14,130 --> 00:19:21,090
Okay, now you're going to insert the flash drive into the usb port...

405
00:19:23,830 --> 00:19:26,140
She calls me moon pie because I'm

406
00:19:26,140 --> 00:19:29,090
Nummy-nummy and she could just eat me up.

407
00:19:30,830 --> 00:19:34,660
Now, please put the flash drive in the usb port.

408
00:19:36,990 --> 00:19:39,960
The one that looks like a little duck's mouth.

409
00:19:41,330 --> 00:19:42,960
Hey, how'd it go?

410
00:19:43,030 --> 00:19:45,360
Terminator broke my phone.

411
00:19:50,860 --> 00:19:52,160
Excuse me.

412
00:19:54,860 --> 00:19:56,090
Okay, I'll be honest with you.

413
00:19:56,160 --> 00:19:59,590
I've just spent the last two hours imagining various scenarios in my head,

414
00:19:59,590 --> 00:20:02,230
Trying to come up with some clever line to say to you.

415
00:20:02,290 --> 00:20:05,460
But then I finally realized you're a human being; I'm a human being.

416
00:20:05,460 --> 00:20:06,790
I could just say to you...

417
00:20:06,860 --> 00:20:08,060
Santa barbara.

418
00:20:08,130 --> 00:20:09,460
I'm sorry. this is me.

419
00:20:12,390 --> 00:20:14,030
Hi, my name's leonard.

420
00:20:18,620 --> 00:20:22,120
So, I'm thinking, you won the nobel prize what, three years ago?

421
00:20:22,190 --> 00:20:25,520
So you must deal with a whole lot of "what has smoot done lately?"

422
00:20:27,120 --> 00:20:31,270
My thought is we continue my research as a team-- you know, cooper-smoot,

423
00:20:31,470 --> 00:20:32,860
you know, cooper-smoot, alphabetical--

424
00:20:33,820 --> 00:20:36,620
and when we win the nobel prize, you'll be back on top.

425
00:20:36,690 --> 00:20:39,950
With all due respect, dr. cooper, are you on crack?

426
00:20:43,790 --> 00:20:46,250
Fine! smoot-cooper.

